From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amirali Abdolrashidi <abdolrashidi@google.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:29:53 -0700
Subject: Vulkan: Include noncoherent atom size alignment

  When flushing or invalidating non-coherent mapped memory ranges
in buffer suballocations, the mapped size must be rounded up to
nonCoherentAtomSize, and the offset must be a multiple of it.
If nonCoherentAtomSize exceeds the default buffer alignment (e.g.
the atom size is 512, but alignment is 256), suballocations could
receive misaligned offsets (VUID-VkMappedMemoryRange-offset-00687).
Additionally, rounding up the size of a suballocation near the end of a
block could cause the range (offset + size) to spill past the memory
block bounds (VUID-VkMappedMemoryRange-size-00685).

In this change, nonCoherentAtomSize is included in determining the
default buffer alignment in order to avoid these errors.

* Added limitsVk.nonCoherentAtomSize as a max argument for
  mDefaultBufferAlignment.

* Updated flush() and invalidate() in BufferSuballocation.

  * Added assertions to make sure the offset is a multiple of
    nonCoherentAtomSize.

  * Fixed the size assertions so the offset is also taken into account
    to make sure the size range is not exceeded.

* Added test: BufferDataTestES3.MapWriteAndReadManySmallDynamicBuffers

Bug: chromium:536599243
Change-Id: I9c5b093a27c3e1fc760c28362c9207bb561abc6f
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8601666
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Charlie Lao <cclao@google.com>

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/Suballocation.cpp b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/Suballocation.cpp
index 637af47e76c3ae4dfa01d9a55f71218b5af00959..4fb459869119f40af53e7eccc3233222206c9712 100644
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/Suballocation.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/Suballocation.cpp
@@ -193,7 +193,8 @@ void BufferSuballocation::flush(Renderer *renderer)
         mappedRange.offset              = getOffset();
         mappedRange.size                = roundUp<VkDeviceSize>(mSize, nonCoherentAtomSize);
 
-        ASSERT(mappedRange.size <= mBufferBlock->getAllocatedBufferSize());
+        ASSERT(mappedRange.offset % nonCoherentAtomSize == 0);
+        ASSERT(mappedRange.offset + mappedRange.size <= mBufferBlock->getAllocatedBufferSize());
         mBufferBlock->getDeviceMemory().flush(renderer->getDevice(), mappedRange);
     }
 }
@@ -211,7 +212,8 @@ void BufferSuballocation::invalidate(Renderer *renderer)
         mappedRange.offset              = getOffset();
         mappedRange.size                = roundUp<VkDeviceSize>(mSize, nonCoherentAtomSize);
 
-        ASSERT(mappedRange.size <= mBufferBlock->getAllocatedBufferSize());
+        ASSERT(mappedRange.offset % nonCoherentAtomSize == 0);
+        ASSERT(mappedRange.offset + mappedRange.size <= mBufferBlock->getAllocatedBufferSize());
         mBufferBlock->getDeviceMemory().invalidate(renderer->getDevice(), mappedRange);
     }
 }
